  "description": "An adventure touring frame stout and stable enough for medium duty touring and bikepacking, but is also nimble enough to be a fun and fast commuter bike. While many modern touring forks only have 3-pack mounts, the Drake’s fork is designed for real racks — mini-rack mounts for randonneuring bags or low rider rack mounts for panniers. The geometry features a unique combination of higher bottom bracket height (higher than on traditional touring and gravel bikes), high stack, and sloping top tube. This helps reduce pedal strike on uneven dirt terrain, allows for a higher bar set-up if desired, and improves standover clearance. It also has plenty of clearance to run plush tires and fenders. Features tried and true standards like English threaded BB shell and QR dropouts and fork ends.\n\nExtra tall headtube makes upright builds look better\n\nSloping top tube for more standover height and more stiffness over level top tube frames\n\nSizing: Virtual sizing -- does not go by seat tube length",
